# Data and large files
#
# DVC pointer files for the reproducible-artifact tiers must stay trackable despite the
# blanket ignores below. Git's rule: "you cannot re-include a file if a parent directory
# of that file is itself excluded" -- a *directory*-level exclusion (matched by a glob
# against its parent, e.g. "data/*" matching the "01_bronze" directory as one of its
# children) blocks git from ever descending into it again, no matter how specific a later
# negation is. So every ancestor directory on the path to an unignored file must itself be
# explicitly un-excluded, in order, before the file-level negation works. See
# docs/DATA_STORAGE.md for what's actually DVC-tracked and why.
host_software/data/*
!host_software/data/01_bronze/
host_software/data/01_bronze/*
# Scoped exception: Track 4 Jetson bronze sessions are DVC-tracked (small, 2 files/session,
# not the ~1M-file bulk legacy bronze data the blanket exclusion above is really for).
!host_software/data/01_bronze/session_jetson_track4_*.dvc
!host_software/data/03_gold.dvc
!host_software/data/03_synthetic_yolo.dvc
!host_software/data/yolo_raw_dataset.dvc
host_software/data_collection/data/

host_software/ml_audio/data/

*.csv
evaluation_results/

generated/
logs/

